WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.360
In this video, you create a Linux virtual machine in SUSE Virtualization from a cloud image, choose how many CPUs and how much memory it gets, and watch it start.

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:14.370
From the Virtual Machines page, select Create.

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:18.970
Choose the namespace the virtual machine belongs to.

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:20.870
Give it a name.

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:23.930
Set two virtual CPUs,

00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:26.580
and four gigabytes of memory.

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:29.910
On the Volumes tab, pick the boot disk.

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:38.510
Select the openSUSE Leap cloud image. The root disk is created from it, ten gigabytes by default.

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:46.650
The Networks tab already has one interface on the management network, which is enough for this virtual machine.

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:50.700
Select Create.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:01:01.410
SUSE Virtualization pulls the image into a volume, schedules the virtual machine, and it is now running with an IP address.

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:05.547
The virtual machine is ready. Next, you open its console.
